ilhão 6, Parque Olímpico da Barra, Barra da Tijuca, Rio de Janeiro"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/356300"} "22 from 22 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Single elimination tournament."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "With " [:a {:href "/athletes/106138"} "Zou Shiming"] " forgoing an attempt to win a third straight title by embarking on a career in the professional ranks, " [:a {:href "/athletes/133362"} "Joahnys Argilagos"] " of Cuba had emerged as a strong favourite to follow in his footsteps as Olympic champion. The Cuban had won the world title in 2015 and, as such, was top seed for Rio. Argilagos survived a close call in his first bout but eventually faltered against a rank outsider, " [:a {:href "/athletes/133259"} "Yurberjen Martínez"] " of Colombia, whose work rate and aggression was preferred by the judges to the swagger and showboating style of the Cuban."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Meanwhile in the bottom half of the draw the Uzbek fighter " [:a {:href "/athletes/136410"} "Hasanboy Dusmatov"] " was fighting his way through a fiendish draw which put him up against top class opponents from Mexico, Kazakhstan and the USA in quick succession. In the final Dusmatov produced the performance of a champion and controlled the fight with a display of counter punching even as the crowd roared the South American forward. One of the judges scored the final round to Martínez or else Dusmatov would have produced a clean sweep of all rounds on all scorecards. Dusmatov promptly dedicated the gold to his country’s president " [:a {:href "/athletes/1200092"} "Islam Karimov"] ". Martínez was the first Colombian boxer to reach an Olympic final."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/136410"} "Hasanboy Dusmatov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "